  "body": "Architecturally striking, impressively proportioned and positioned in one of Auckland's most desirable bays neighbourhoods, this substantial 280sqm (approx.) freehold residence delivers an enviable lifestyle without the demands of a large section.\r\n\r\nBuilt in 2009, this distinctive cedar and weatherboard home combines soaring raked ceilings, rich timber floors, extensive glazing and a north-west facing aspect to create beautifully light-filled interiors with an elevated outlook.\r\n\r\nDesigned for entertaining, expansive living and dining areas flow effortlessly to the outdoors. The generous kitchen, featuring an expansive stone island, stainless-steel appliances and gas cooking, is a natural gathering point.\r\n\r\nFour double bedrooms and multiple living areas provide exceptional flexibility. Two bedrooms and a separate family room open directly to the landscaped gardens, complemented by a family bathroom and guest powder room. Upstairs, the generous master suite boasts a large walk-in wardrobe and stylish ensuite with twin basins, alongside a fourth bedroom. A carpeted double internal-access garage, excellent storage, additional off-street parking and easy-care grounds complete the package.\r\n\r\nAnd then there's the location. Beaches, coastal cafes, Kepa Bush Reserve and Eastridge Shopping Centre are all just moments away, with zoning for Orakei School and Selwyn College.\r\n\r\nWhether you're upsizing or seeking an effortless lock-up-and-leave lifestyle, this home delivers space, style and location in equal measure.\r\n\r\nFor more info, call John & Jane 0800 ORAKEI",
